 "heard": "McDonald's is a landlord that happens to sell burgers. It has more than 45,000 restaurants, but it runs only about one in 20 of them. About 95% belong to franchisees. They hire the staff and run the kitchens. So how does McDonald's get paid? Twice a. First, a royalty, a cut of every sale. Last year that came to $6 billion. Second rent. McDonald's usually owns or leases the land and the building. The franchisee pays rent to use them, month after month. Last year rent came to $10.4 billion. That is far more than the royalties. Selling burgers is the franchisee's job. Collecting rent is McDonald's job. In its main markets, it owns about 56% of the land and 80% of the buildings. Menus change. Prices change. The landlord still gets paid which is why.",
